{
  "_README": [
    "OPTION CONSTRAINTS — one sentence per option saying how choosing it narrows",
    "the NEXT step of the round. Authored content, not code: edit this file and",
    "the sentence changes. No deploy needed beyond the usual restart.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS. During the strategic decision a team does not need the",
    "business-unit table — twenty-eight numbers that answer a different question.",
    "They need to know what their choice makes possible and what it forecloses.",
    "This is the sentence a facilitator says standing behind them.",
    "",
    "HOW TO WRITE ONE.",
    "  1. Lead with the consequence, not the reasoning: which units, or what",
    "     capability, is open or closed after this choice.",
    "  2. One sentence, two at most. It sits under the option cards, not in them.",
    "  3. Say what is LOST as well as what is gained — a team that cannot see the",
    "     road not taken learns nothing from taking one.",
    "  4. Plain English. No ESRS clause numbers, no engine variable names.",
    "  5. Wrap the load-bearing clause in <b>…</b>. Nothing else renders as HTML.",
    "",
    "EMPTY IS SAFE. An empty string renders no constraint line at all — the",
    "decision screen simply shows the options and the comparison table, exactly as",
    "it does today. Author the rounds you have taught; leave the rest until you",
    "have watched them run.",
    "",
    "KEYS MUST MATCH detailed_descriptions.json exactly. The jest tripwire",
    "frontend/__tests__/option-constraints-drift.test.js fails the build if the two",
    "files disagree, or if the frontend mirror drifts from this file."
  ],
